hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"323","Ours is Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein, Ahmad bin Sinan Al-Wasiti, and Musa bin Khaqan al-Baghdadi said: Ishaq, who is the son of Yusuf al-Azraq, told us, and this is the hadith of al-Dawraqi, narrated by Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Marthad, on the authority of Suleiman bin Buraydah, on the authority of his father, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about the time for the prayers. He said: Pray with us, so when When the sun had passed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the noon prayer and said: He prayed the afternoon prayer while the sun was high and pure, and he prayed the sunset prayer when the sun had set. He prayed the evening prayer when twilight had disappeared, and he prayed the dawn prayer while sitting, and the next day he ordered Bilal to call the noon call to prayer, and he cooled off with it, and he was blessed to be cooled off. And He commanded him, so he established the afternoon prayer while the sun was alive. He delayed it beyond what it was, and he commanded him, so he established the sunset before twilight had set, and he commanded him So he performed the Ishaa’ prayer after a third of the night had passed, and he commanded him to perform the Fajr Iqama, and he carried it out, then he said: “Where is the one who asked about the time for prayer?” He said: It is me, O Messenger of God. He said: “The time of your prayer is between what you have seen.” Abu Bakr said: I did not find in my book on the authority of Al-Zafarani the sunset on that day. The second"
"324","Abu Tahir informed us, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Bundar, on the authority of Harami ibn Amara, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Marthad, on the authority of Suleiman. Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the appointed times, Bundar did not add anything to this. Bundar said: So I mentioned it to Abu Dawud, and he said: The author of this hadith should say “Allahu Akbar” for him. Bundar said: So I erased it from my book. Abu Bakr said: Abu Dawud should be glorified where he made a mistake, and Bundar should be beaten ten times. He erased this hadith from his book. It is an authentic hadith based on what Al-Thawri also narrated on the authority of Alqamah. Abu Dawud made a mistake, and Bundar changed this hadith. Authentic. It was also narrated by Al-Thawri on the authority of Alqamah with the news of Harami bin Amara Muhammad bin Yahya, who said: Narrated by Ali bin Abdullah, narrated by Harami bin Amara, On the authority of Shu`bah, with the entire hadith, Abu Bakr said: This news is a response to the Iraqis’ claim that the one who decided with the ruler was in charge of so-and-so. Between one dirham and ten dirhams, he owed eight dirhams, so they made this part of the article into a long section, and they divided issues on this topic. The error that fuels their article requires that Gabriel led the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on two days and two nights, the five prayers other than Its timing; Because the basis of their argument is that the times of prayer are between the first time and the second time, and that the first and second time are outside of The time for prayer is as they claim that the dirham and ten are outside of what the one who declared it acknowledged, and that the eight is between one dirham and ten, I have dictated A long question of this kind."
